      "caption": "Fig. 2\n\nFGFR1 promotes growth of ER+ BC cells in co-culture systems modeling interactions with the brain microenvironment.\n\na IHC of pFGFR1 and FGFR1 in 48 ER+ BCBM samples (left) and membrane expression mask (right) performed using the Digital Imaging Aperio algorithm for membrane-expression. Images are representative of masking strategy for all 48 samples. Right: Spearman correlation of pFGFR1 and FGFR1 membrane expression. b BM frequency, FGFR amplification status, and FGFR1 relative mRNA (FPKM) for ER+ cells. c FGFR1 and pFGFR1 immunoblots in ER+ BC cell lines. The samples derive from the same experiment but different gels for FGFR1 and another for pFGFR1 and GAPDH were processed in parallel. d FGFR1 immunoblot in shNC and shFGFR1 UCD65 and UCD12 cells. Numbers indicate GAPDH-normalized expression relative to shNC. Images in (c, d) are representative of three independent immunoblots. Time course growth of shNC and shFGFR1 UCD65 (e) and UCD12 cells (f\nn = 10 biological replicates per condition) in E2-free media, treated with vehicle (EtOH) or 10 nM E2. Confluence measured via Incucyte imaging every 12 hours, normalized to time 0. g Schematic of organotypic coculture. UCD65 shNC (n = 14) and shFGFR1 (shFGFR1 #1 n = 17, shFGFR1 #2 n = 12) spheroids (h), and UCD12 shNC (n = 18) and shFGFR1 (shFGFR1 #1 n = 19, shFGFR1 #2 n = 18) spheroids (i) were growth on young (9–13w) organotypic brain slices; UCD65 shNC (n = 8) and shFGFR1 (shFGFR1 #1 n = 7, shFGFR1 #2 n = 8) spheroids (j), and UCD12 shNC (n = 16) and shFGFR1 (shFGFR1 #1 n = 15, shFGFR1 #2 n = 16) spheroids (k, p = 8.99E-05) were grown on aged (49-53w) organotypic brain slices. Graphs show change in GFP intensity per spheroid over time corrected for background fluorescence, normalized to day 1. l FGFR1 immunoblot in MCF7 FGFR1-OE and EV cells, representative of three independent immunoblots. m Fold change growth measured by SRB assay of MCF7 FGFR1-OE and EV cells after 6 days of treatment with 10 nM E2 or EtOH vehicle (n = 5 biological replicates per condition). Growth of MCF7-EV spheroids (n = 16 on young, n = 18 on aged) and MCF7-FGFR1-OE spheroids (n = 17 on young, n = 15 on aged) on organotypic slices from a young (13w) (n, p = 2.10E-05) or aged (45w) (o) NSG mouse. For e, f, h–k, n, o lines denote mean ± SEM and data were analyzed with 2-way ANOVA followed by Fisher’s LSD test. Data in m were analyzed by 1-way ANOVA with Fisher’s LSD test, and error bars denote SEM. All scale bars are 500 µm. *:p < 0.05. For e E2 vs EtOH: UCD65 shNC p = 5.46E-04, shFGFR1 #1 p = 1.11E-08, shFGFR1 #2 p = 4.03E-08; for f, UCD12 shNC p = 1.10E-11, shFGFR1 #1 p = 2.96E-10, shFGFR1 #2 p = 1.83E-10. Source data are provided as a Source Data file. h Created in BioRender. Cittelly, D. (https://BioRender.com/hbdv1ya).",
