      "figure": "Fig. 5",
      "caption": "Fig. 5\n\nAstrocytes promote canonical FGF2-dependent activation of FGFR1 in ER+ BC.\n\na FGF2 ELISA from total brain, oligodendrocyte (OL, p = 6.04E-04), microglia, neuron, and astrocyte lysates isolated from young (12 weeks) and aged ( > 56 weeks) female mice (n = 3). b FGF2 ELISA from young (mAst P0, 15 days in vitro) and aged (Aged mAst, 90 days in vitro) mouse primary astrocyte lysates (n = 4). c Immunofluorescence of GFAP and FGF2 in mAst-P0 and aged-mAst. Images are representative of three biological replicates and two independent stainings. d Immunofluorescence of pFGFR1 in UCD65 alone or co-cultured with mAst-P0 and aged-mAst in serum-free media. Right: pFGFR1 Corrected Total Cell Fluorescence in UCD65 (n = 4–6 biological replicates per group, Alone vs mAst-P0 p = 2.49E-06). e Schematic of the experimental design for co-cultures of UCD65 shEV and shFGFR1 cells with mAst-P0 or aged-mAst. f Fold change in total green area relative to time 0 of UCD65 shEV and shFGFR1 cells cultured alone or with mAst-P0 or Aged-mAst in E2-free media (n = 3 biological replicates per condition, all comparisons p < 1.00E-15), measured by Incucyte. g Representative images of the three wells per condition at 18 days. h Schematic of organotypic co-cultures with neutralizing antibodies. i Spheroids of GFP+ UCD12 cells (n = 10 per condition) were plated on organotypic brain slices from a young (8w) NSG mouse. Slices were pretreated for 24 h with 1 µg anti-FGF2 blocking antibody or IgG control. Graph shows change in GFP intensity per spheroid over time corrected for background fluorescence, normalized to day 1. p = 3.97E-12. For a, b data were analyzed with two-sided t-tests, and error bars denote SEM. d was analyzed with 1-way ANOVA followed by Fisher’s LSD test. For f, i line denotes mean ± SEM, data were analyzed with 2-way ANOVA followed by Fisher’s LSD test. P values shown for last time point only. Source data are provided as a Source Data file. e Created in BioRender. Cittelly, D. (https://BioRender.com/gjirwho). h Created in BioRender. Cittelly, D. (https://BioRender.com/ynafhdx).",
