      "figure": "Fig. 3",
      "caption": "Fig. 3\n\nA HUVECs were stimulated with ECVEnic or control (EBM-2) for 12 hours (incubation). Then, 100 ng/ml LPS with co-factors LBP and CD14 or co-factors alone (sham) were added and incubated for another 18 hours. Created in BioRender. Stahl, K. (2026) https://BioRender.com/nu4iwxz. B Angpt-2 concentrations in the supernatant were measured by ELISA when LPS was added as well as 12 and 18 hours after LPS or sham stimulation and are shown over time. Each group consisted of n=6. Mixed ANOVA with according post-tests were performed. C 18 hours after stimulation with LPS or sham Angpt-2 mRNA transcription was measured by qPCR. Each group consisted of n=9. D Additionally, the Angpt-2/Tie2 mRNA ratio is shown after initial ECVEnic incubation and 18 hours of LPS or sham stimulation. ECVEnic / sham consisted of n=8, all other groups consisted of n=9. Groups were analyzed by Kruskal-Wallis test with post-hoc Dunn test. E TER was measured at different time points by an ECIS system. HUVECs were pre-incubated with ECVEnic (n=7) or control (n=8) for 12 hours. Then half of the medium was changed and cells were stimulated with LPS. Results are shown as dot plots with mean ± SD. A linear mixed-effects model was used for analysis. P-values < 0.05 are considered significant. Abbreviations: Angpt-2 - Angiopoietin-2, ECIS - Electric cell-substrate impedance sensing, ECVE – e-cigarette vapor extract, HUVECs – human umbilical vein endothelial cells, LPS - lipopolysaccharide, SD – standard deviation, TER – transendothelial electrical resistance",
