      "caption": "Fig. 4\n\nA A schematic setup is shown for stimulation with the Tie2 agonist PMC-403 and its effects on HUVECs and HPMECs, accordingly. Created in BioRender. Stahl, K. (2026) https://BioRender.com/yc7s3fj. B HUVECs were stimulated with different concentrations of the Tie2 agonist PMC-403 or 500 ng/ml Angpt-1 for 1 hour. A western blot was performed and pAKT and AKT were analyzed. C HPMECs were incubated with 1 µg/ml PMC-403 for 1 hour and then stimulated with LPS. TER was measured by ECIS over time and group differences over time were analyzed by a linear mixed-effects model accordingly. D Group differences are shown 6.5 hours after LPS stimulation. Results are shown as dot plots with mean ± SD and each group consisted of n=4. P-values < 0.05 are considered significant. Abbreviations: Angpt-1 - Angiopoietin-1, ECIS - Electric cell-substrate impedance sensing, HPMECs - human pulmonary microvascular endothelial cells, HUVECs – human umbilical vein endothelial cells, LPS - lipopolysaccharide, SD – standard deviation, TER – transendothelial electrical resistance",
