      "caption": "Fig. 4.\n\nA CRISPRi genome-wide screen identifies genes essential for CH4-dependent growth.\n\n(A) Schematic workflow for methanotroph CRISPRi library construction. (B) Growth of the CRISPRi library cultivated in 20% CH4 in air atmosphere with or without sgRNA and dCas9 induction. a.u., arbitrary units. (C) Circos plot of the methanotroph sgRNA library raw reads (outer ring) mapped to the 45,798 synthesized sgRNA oligos (rainbow ring with nontargeting sgRNAs in blue). Differential sgRNA fitness scores determined via DESeq2 between CRISPRi induced (n = 4) and uninduced (n = 4) samples during selection/cultivation with CH4 as the sole carbon and energy source (fourth ring, blue dots: log2 > 1; red dots: log2 < 1). sgRNAs depleted in the screen correspond to genes with transcription repression causing a growth defect where those enriched correspond to genes with transcription repression causing a growth advantage. sgRNAs with statistically significant (P ≤ 0.01) differential fitness scores are indicated (blue squares, third ring). (D) ShinyGO enrichment analysis of the 699 genes with sgRNA log2 fitness scores ≤ −1 and P ≤ 0.001. The 10 pathways with the lowest false discovery rates, sorted by the number of genes are shown. (E) CH4 assimilatory and dissimilatory metabolic pathways predicted by sgRNA fitness scores. The mean sgRNA fitness scores are indicated in parentheses next to the gene loci that encode metabolic enzymes. Scores with P ≥ 0.01 are italicized. 3PG, 3-phosphoglycerate; G3P, glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate; F1,6P, fructose 1,6-bisphosphate; F6P, fructose 6-phosphate; E4P, erythrose 4-phosphate; Xu5P, xylulose 5-phosphate; S7P, sedoheptulose 7-phosphate; R5P, ribose 5-phosphate; Ru5P, ribulose 5-phosphate; R1,5P, ribulose 1,5-bisphosphate; G6P, glucose-6-phosphate; 6PG, 6-phosphogluconate; KDPG, 2-keto-3-deoxy-6-phosphogluconate; Pyr, pyruvate; CH2═H4F, methylene-tetrahydrofolate; CH2═H4MPT, methylene-tetrahydromethanopterin; CH≡H4F, methenyl-tetrahydrofolate; CH≡H4MPT, methenyl-tetrahydromethanopterin; CHO-H4F, formyl-tetrahydrofolate; CHO-H4MPT, formyl-tetrahydromethanopterin. Data in (B) represent the mean of two independent high-resolution cultivation experiments (n = 6). (A) and (E) were created in BioRender. Henard, C. (2026) https://BioRender.com/57nyxu5; https://BioRender.com/p4flgui.",
