      "authors": "Ilaria Cislaghi; Sarah Turati; Dalila Vicario; Gloria Griffante; Shikha Chandel; Irene Lo Cigno; Ranieri Bizzarri; Barbara Storti; Tina Ukmar Godec; Milan Zachrdla; Markus Zweckstetter; Lucia Signorini; Kevin Kamau Maina; Serena Delbue; Cinzia Borgogna; Marisa Gariglio",
      "figure": "Fig. 6",
      "caption": "Fig. 6\n\nThe IFI16 protein also impairs OC43 replication but promotes NL63 replication.\n\nTC and IFI16KO cells were infected with OC43 (a) or NL63 (b) at an MOI of 0.01 and 1, respectively. Cell-free supernatants were harvested at the indicated hpi, and the absolute quantification of viral RNA was determined by ddPCR. Data are presented as mean ± SD (two-way ANOVA, *p < 0.05, ****p < 0.0001, n = 3 biological replicates). c Schematic representation of the N proteins of the seven HCoVs. The following domains are highlighted: N-terminal domain (NTD), C-terminal domain (CTD), and intrinsically disordered region (IDR). Created with BioRender.com licensed under CC BY 4.0. https://BioRender.com/6hvfilx.",
