      "authors": "Eleni Papachristoforou; Kexin Kong; Fabio Colella; Jacky Tam; Juliet Luft; Ravi Parhar; Yingxin Liang; Ailish McCafferty-Brown; George Finney; Keshav Rao; Jayamary Divya Ravichandar; Elena F. Sutherland; Stefan Veizades; Malgorzata Grzelka; Pak Kwan Qiu; Ayma Asif; Ines Battle; Max Hammer; Theresa Kuschnereit; Raktaprabal Kashyap; Sebastian J. Wallace; John R. Wilson-Kanamori; Ginerva Pistocchi; Tabitha Turner-Stokes; Alvile Kasarinaite; Josepmaria Argemi; Elisa Pose; Ramon Bataller; David Lopez; Anna Zagorska; Grant Budas; Gareth-Rhys Jones; Calum C. Bain; Catalina A. Vallejos; Ashis Mukhopadhya; Neil C. Henderson; David C. Hay; James C. Lee; Laura J. Pallett; Volker M. Lauschke; Timothy J. Kendall; Jonathan A. Fallowfield; Prakash Ramachandran",
      "figure": "Fig. 7",
      "caption": "Fig. 7\n\nTargeting OLR1+ MDMs attenuates fibrogenic activity.\n\na, Genes coexpressed with OLR1 across 67 monocyte/macrophage activation conditions, ranked by Pearson correlation coefficient. Selected genes are highlighted. b, Genes coexpressed with GPNMB across 67 monocyte/macrophage activation conditions, ranked by Pearson correlation coefficient. Selected genes are highlighted. c, GSVA enrichment scores for 67 different monocyte/macrophage activation conditions to identify stimuli that phenocopy SAMac1 or SAMac2 gene sets derived from liver scRNA-seq data. Selected activation stimuli are highlighted. d, Scaled gene expression for selected genes across 67 different monocyte/macrophage activation conditions. Selected activation stimuli are highlighted. e, qPCR of primary human MDMs (n = 10) showing effects of TPP stimulation on expression of selected genes shown as log2(FC) relative to expression in control samples. Dots represent separate patients. Bars indicate mean ± s.e.m. Two-sided Wilcoxon matched-pairs signed-rank test for each gene versus control; *P < 0.05, **P < 0.01 (OLR1\nP = 0.0371; IL1B\nP = 0.0020; GPNMB\nP = 0.0020). f, Overview of experimental workflow for assessing effect of MDM OLR1 modulation on HSC fibrogenic activity. g, Relative COL1A1 and COL3A1 mRNA expression of LX2 HSCs after incubation with conditioned media from primary MDMs (n = 6 patients) pretreated with OLR1 targeting or control siRNA. Boxes are min-to-max expression with line at mean. Dots connected by lines represent data from MDMs of six different patients with CLD. Two-sided ratio paired t test, *P < 0.05 (P = 0.0291 for COL1A1; P = 0.0532 for COL3A1). h, Relative COL1A1 and COL3A1 mRNA expression of LX2 HSCs after incubation with conditioned media from primary MDMs pretreated with OLR1 blocking antibody (MEDI6570) or isotype control antibody. Boxes are min-to-max expression with line at mean. Dots connected by lines represent data from MDMs of four different patients with CLD. Two-sided ratio paired t test, *P < 0.05 (P = 0.0496 for COL1A1; P = 0.0218 for COL3A1). i, Overview of experimental workflow for assessing effects of OLR1 modulation on fibrogenic activity in primary human 3D multilineage spheroids after MASH induction by FFA. Schematics in f and i created in BioRender: f, Colella, F. https://BioRender.com/l42u16a (2025); i, Colella, F. https://BioRender.com/pjoyobq (2026). j, qPCR of MASH spheroids (n = 3) treated with OLR1 or control siRNA. Dots represent different spheroid cultures. Expression of stated gene in each OLR1 siRNA-treated spheroid culture relative to control siRNA-treated spheroid. Bars indicate mean ± s.e.m. Two-sided Welsh’s t test; *P < 0.05 (P = 0.0106). k, qPCR of COL1A1 and COL3A1 in lean spheroids (no FFA treatment) and MASH primary liver spheroids treated with OLR1 or control siRNA. Dots represent different spheroid cultures, n = 5 per group. Bars indicate mean ± s.e.m. One-way ANOVA with Dunnett’s multiple comparison test; *P < 0.05, **P < 0.01, ***P < 0.001. l, ELISA for pro-collagen 1 from lean spheroids (n = 12) and MASH primary liver spheroids treated with OLR1 (n = 12) or control (n = 14) siRNA. Dots represent different spheroid cultures. One-way ANOVA with Dunnett’s multiple comparison test; ****P < 0.0001. ANOVA, analysis of variance; GSVA, gene set variation analysis.\n\nSource data",
