      "figure": "Extended Data Fig. 8",
      "caption": "Extended Data Fig. 8\n\nDissecting SAMac origin and kinetics in mouse CLD.\n\na, Flow cytometry gating strategy for study of SAMac kinetics in mouse liver. Cells were pregated as viable (DAPI negative) singlets (based on FSC-A versus FSC-H and SSC-A versus SSC-H). Identified SAMac population is then gated for OLR1 and CD319 expression as shown Fig. 5g. b, Overview of experimental workflow for mouse bone marrow chimera CLD model. Wild-type mice (CD45.2+) were used as recipients and CD45.1+ mice as bone marrow donors. Schematic in b created in BioRender; Colella, F. https://BioRender.com/fnfo96e (2025). HSC, hematopoietic stem cell. c, Flow cytometry gating strategy for bone marrow chimera studies to quantitate macrophage subpopulation chimerism in mouse liver. Cells were pregated as viable (DAPI negative) singlets (based on FSC-A versus FSC-H and SSC-A versus SSC-H) and monocyte-macrophages defined as shown in a. The gated macrophage subpopulations shown were then all assessed for the degree of chimerism (% CD45.1+). MDM, monocyte-derived macrophage; KC, Kupffer cell; moKC, monocyte-derived Kupffer cell. d, Bar plot of degree of chimerism of liver macrophage subpopulations, quantitated by flow cytometry of uninjured mice (n = 5) following the busulfan chimera protocol. Bars indicate mean ± s.d. with individual dots representing independent mice. Normalized chimerism calculated for each mouse by normalizing to the % of peripheral blood monocytes which are donor-derived (CD45.1+). Ordinary one-way ANOVA with Tukey’s multiple comparisons test; ****P < 0.0001. e, Bar plot of degree of chimerism of liver macrophage subpopulations, quantitated by flow cytometry of chronic CCl4 treated mice (n = 4) following the busulfan chimera protocol. Bars indicate mean ± s.d. with individual dots representing independent mice. Normalized chimerism calculated for each mouse by normalizing to the % of peripheral blood monocytes that are donor-derived (CD45.1+). Ordinary one-way ANOVA with Tukey’s multiple comparisons test. ****P < 0.0001.\n\nSource data",
