      "caption": "Extended Data Fig. 6\n\nPharmacological inhibition of Mitochondrial Citrate Carrier (SLC25A1) reduces the SASP without affecting other hallmarks of senescence.\n\n(a) Heatmap of cytokine array data from 24-h conditioned media, presented as the average of n = 3 independent experiments per condition. (b-d) Quantification of (b) nuclear HMGB1 mean intensity per nucleus, (c) mean number of γH2A.X foci per nucleus, and (d) percentage of Ki67-positive proliferating cells in proliferative, senescent, and CTPI2-treated senescent cells ((b) n = 4 Prol and Sen(IR), n = 3 Sen(IR) + CTPI2, (c) n = 8, (d) n = 4). (e) Representative immunofluorescence images of HMGB1 and γH2A.X staining in different conditions. Scale bar = 50 μm. (f) Western blot showing reduced histone acetylation (H3K9ac) following CTPI-2 treatment (representative from n = 3). (g) Schematic illustrating the 13C-glucose tracing experimental approach. Created in BioRender; Martini, H. https://biorender.com/u87b9lc (2026). (h) Percentage of 13C incorporation into H3K9ac after 24 h in irradiation-induced senescent cells (Sen(IR)) treated with or without CTPI-2 (n = 3). nd, not detected. Data are presented as mean ± s.e.m. Statistical analyses were performed using one-way ANOVA with Tukey’s multiple comparison test. (n = independent experiment). P-values as indicated in the figure. ns = non significant p > 0.05.\n\nSource data",
