      "caption": "FIGURE 1\n\nDesign rationale and therapeutic mechanism of PCN for aged PND. (A) Schematic illustration of the construction of a homologous neutrophil membrane‐camouflaged Pd/hCeO2 nanoplatform (PCN). (B) Following intravenous administration, PCN leverages innate neutrophil inflammatory chemotaxis to traverse the disrupted BBB and preferentially accumulate in inflamed cerebrovascular and parenchymal regions. (C) In the aging brain, PCN modulates microglial inflammatory and metabolic states, attenuates oxidative stress and neuroinflammation, preserves synaptic structure and BBB integrity, and ultimately improves cognitive function in aged PND mice. Figure 1 was created in BioRender. Huang, L. (2026) https://BioRender.com/u8g59kf.",
