      "caption": "Fig. 5\n\nDeletion of the IG-TRE∆550 in vivo is viable and results in decreased maternal gene expression in adult brains.\n\nA Breeding strategy of the IG-TRE 550 bp deletion animals crossed with C57BL/6 partners to produce maternal or paternal inheritance of the IG-TRE∆550 deletion. In each litter, 50% of the pups are wild-type littermates (pure C57BL/6) and kept as controls. Tissues were collected for expression at 9 weeks. Created in BioRender. Edwards, C. (2026) https://BioRender.com/y4zqy25. B Box plot representation of total body weight (g) of 9-week-old adult animals. For WT, ∆P TRE∆550 and ∆M TRE∆550 males: Min = 24, 26, 23.9; Q1 = 25.4, 26.1, 25.2; Center line= 26.8, 26.3, 26.4; Q3 = 27.8, 27.5, 27.7; Max= 29.7, 29.1, 29.1; n = 22, 5, 13. For WT, ∆P TRE∆550 and ∆M TRE∆550 females: Min = 16.3, 19.2, 19.2; Q1 = 19.2, 19.5, 19.5; Center line = 19.7, 20.3, 20.1; Q3 = 20.7, 20.5, 20.8; Max= 22.4, 22, 23.3; n = 16, 5, 8. C Box plot representation of total body length (cm) of 9-week-old adult animals. For WT, ∆P TRE∆550 and ∆M TRE∆550 males: Min= 9, 8.9, 9.2; Q1 = 9.1, 9.2, 9.6; Center line = 9.5, 9.5, 9.8; Q3 = 9.9, 9.5, 9.9; Max= 10, 10, 10; n = 22, 5, 13. For WT, ∆P TRE∆550 and ∆M TRE∆550 females: Min= 8.5, 8.5, 8.5; Q1 = 8.6, 9, 8.9; Center line = 9.1, 9, 9.1; Q3 = 9.5, 9.1, 9.4; Max= 10.8, 9.2, 9.8; n = 16, 5, 8. D Breeding strategy of IG-TREΔ550 females crossed with CAST/EiJ males to produce hybrid animals with maternal inheritance of the IG-TREΔ550 deletion. In each litter, 50% of the pups are wild-type littermates (hybrid BxC) and kept as controls. Tissues were collected for expression at 9 weeks. Created in BioRender. Edwards, C. (2026) https://BioRender.com/b9fvzre. E Graphical representation of the relative expression of the Dlk1-Dio3 genes, as measured by qPCR, in adult brains of maternal IG-TREΔ550 and BxC wild-type littermates (PGtl2 = 0.001, PRian = 1.3E−06, PMirg = 0.001). F Graphical representation of the allelic expression of the Dlk1-Dio3 genes, as measured by pyro SNP analysis, in adult brains of maternal IG-TREΔ550 and BxC wild-type littermates (PDlk1 = 3.5E−10). Expression analysis shows that Dlk1 maternal expression is increased, and Gtl2, Rian, and Mirg are decreased in maternal IG-TREΔ550 adult brains. nWTBC = 10, n∆M-TRE∆550 = 15 biologically independent adult brains were analyzed for gene expression. Data are presented as mean values +/− SEM. NS not significant. Asterisks indicate statistical significance in comparison to wild-type using a two-tailed unpaired Student’s t test.",
