      "caption": "Fig. 4.\n\nRoles and mechanisms of action of camalexin in the interaction of A. thaliana with microbes. Beneficial microbes are drawn in blue and pathogens are drawn in red. Solid arrows represent known pathways, and dashed arrows represent proposed or not fully defined pathways. Interactions with pathogens are shown at the left side of the main panel, and interactions with beneficial microbes are shown at the right side. Internal panels show (A) the regulatory network of the master phytoalexin transcription factor WRKY33 upon sensing of microbe-associated molecular patterns (MAMPs), (B) the known camalexin resistance and detoxification mechanisms of select fungal pathogens, and (C) the hypothesized toxicity mechanisms of camalexin against bacterial and fungal pathogens. Abbreviations: PGPM, plant growth-promoting microbes; CBP, camalexin biosynthetic pathway. Created in BioRender. Elkatmis, B. (2026) https://BioRender.com/j2ubbp3.",
