      "id": "433c07a0",
      "diagram": "diagram/433c07a0.png",
      "class": "Conceptual Framework",
      "domain": "1",
      "title": "Hospital sinks and healthcare-associated infection: ecology, transmission, surveillance and mitigation",
      "authors": "Aoife Kearney; Kevin Chau; Shireen Kotay; Jessica Martin; Andrew Kirby; Amy J Mathers; Nicole Stoesser",
      "figure": "Fig. 1",
      "caption": "Fig. 1\n\nThe microbial epidemiology of sink-traps is driven by various biotic and abiotic factors which may be static or dynamic. The environment directly within the sink-trap includes the microbial population (both planktonic, in the liquid within the trap, and biofilm adhered to the trap surface), the structure of the trap and residual substances (e.g. antimicrobials, disinfectants) contained within. Microbiota present within the trap arise both from sink-use (contributed by patients, healthcare workers etc.) and migration from within the wider water distribution and wastewater plumbing network. The ecology of the sink-trap is additionally modified by the design, placement, function and use of the sink. Each sink is connected to a wider plumbing system, which supplies water to the tap and removes waste from the trap to the wider system. This plumbing system is supplied by a local water source, and the quality, distribution method and WASH indicators relating to this varies. Created in BioRender. Kearney, A. (2026) https://BioRender.com/56iolxa.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ebiom.2026.106415",
      "license": "CC BY 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
      "condition": "Specific BioRender page explicitly licenses this Completed Graphic under CC BY 4.0; individual BioRender icons may not be extracted and redistributed separately. Article permissions cover the saved author text under CC BY 4.0. Selected excerpts and captions contain no identified credit requiring separate permission. Other article images are omitted. Image bytes unchanged; complete BioRender public PNG, no cropping or icon extraction. Original-language article paragraphs and linked captions converted from JATS XML to Markdown; styling removed, no OCR, translation or paraphrase. Graphic: Figure 1. Creator: Aoife Kearney. Provider: BioRender. Asset source: https://biorender.com/56iolxa. License evidence: https://app.biorender.com/citation/6a746c56f99877141c3ba88b. “Figure 1” created in BioRender. Kearney, A. (https://BioRender.com/56iolxa) is licensed under CC BY 4.0. Article caption explicitly links to the complete BioRender asset; may correspond to a panel or construction sheet rather than the entire published figure.",
