      "id": "8fcec9d1",
      "diagram": "diagram/8fcec9d1.png",
      "class": "Conceptual Framework",
      "domain": "1",
      "title": "Hospital sinks and healthcare-associated infection: ecology, transmission, surveillance and mitigation",
      "authors": "Aoife Kearney; Kevin Chau; Shireen Kotay; Jessica Martin; Andrew Kirby; Amy J Mathers; Nicole Stoesser",
      "figure": "Fig. 5",
      "caption": "Fig. 5\n\nSink risk mitigation strategies. Strategies described in the literature typically involve sink removal, replacement or upgrades of plumbing fixtures, mandating regular flushing regimens, cleaning or disinfection or attempt to modify sink-use behaviours. There remains no agreement in the literature on which approach is broadly implementable, feasible and evidence-based; each approach has distinct opportunities and potential advantages, though challenges have been reported for each. Created in BioRender. Kearney, A. (2026) https://BioRender.com/wu3pstu.",
