      "caption": "Fig. 2\n\nThe villus bottom epithelium exhibits a transcriptional shift towards maturity and innate immunity at day 3 post-IR.\n\na Log2 expression of monocyte markers Ccl2 and Lyz2; increased expression from D0 to D3 post-IR, rep2. b Five epithelial clusters (villus-tip, upper villus, bottom villus, crypt-villus junction and crypt) across all timepoints, rep2; k-means clustering restricted to epithelial bins. The post-mitotic villus-bottom cells (green, D0) are absent at D3 and replaced by a cluster associated with the upper villus at D0 (yellow). Similar clustering observed in rep3 and rep4 (Supplementary Fig. 3a). c Percent distribution of epithelial clusters, all timepoints and replicates; proportion of epithelial bins per cluster normalized to total epithelial bins per sample. n = 5 (D0), 3(D1), 3(D2), 3(D3), 2(D4), 3(D5), 1(D6); 2 of D4 samples included. Error bars: SEM across all replicates. d GSEA of differential expression between D3 and D0 bottom-villus clusters (MNA > 0.05) against Moor et al.17 zonation gene sets. The villus-tip gene set (zone 5) is enriched in D3 villus epithelium, and the bottom-villus set (zone 2) in D0. e Spatiotemporal expression (log2-transformed UMI) of zonation markers Lamb3 (zone 5) and Aadac (zone 2) in D0 and D3 post-IR. f Schematic of EdU-based proliferation assay. Mice received EdU at days 2.5 and 3.5 post-IR; tissues collected 24-h later. n = 2 per timepoint (control, D3.5, D4.5). Created in BioRender. Ofer, R. (2026) https://BioRender.com/5gyb85y. g 24-h EdU pulse-chase reveals retention of proliferative epithelial cells in crypts at day 3.5 post-IR followed by upward migration by day 4.5, suggesting delayed new-cell contribution to the villus base during regeneration. EdU and DAPI counterstain; n = 2 mice per condition. h DEG, bottom villus cluster, D0 vs. D3; representative GO terms shown. DEG criteria: log2FC > 1, adj. P < 0.05, MNA > 0.03; GO calculated in DAVID73,74, (modified Fisher’s exact test (EASE score), Benjamini–Hochberg correction. Full gene list and GO results in Supplementary Data 5. i Spatiotemporal expression (log2-transformed UMI) of Rdh7, Alpk1 across post-IR timepoints. Scale bar: 200 µm (a, e, i); 100 µm (b, g, h). Source data are provided as a Source Data file.",
