      "authors": "Rachel Ofer; Tyler Tran; Ping He; Xia Qiu; Xinyu Hu; Emmanuel Zachariah; Curtis Krier; Ankit Saxena; Lei Chen; Jiekun Yang; Michael P Verzi",
      "figure": "Fig. 5",
      "caption": "Fig. 5\n\nSpatial transcriptomics reveals regional signaling dynamics during regeneration and provides insight into stromal-epithelial interactions.\n\na Stromal regions are defined by unsupervised graph-based clustering (rep2); villus stroma, inter-crypt stroma, and sub-crypt stroma. b GO enrichment in day 0 tissues reveals distinct biological functions for each stromal domain. Full gene list and GO results in Supplementary Data 9. c Proportional representation of the stromal regions across days 0, 3 and 5 post-IR. d Stromal domains identified at day 3 and day 5 post-IR by graph-based clustering used for GO term analyses in (e) and (f). Colors represent villus, inter-crypt, or sub-crypt stromal clusters. e, f GO term enrichment in villus stroma (e) and inter-crypt stroma (f) reveals upregulation of immune activation and tissue repair pathways at days 3 and 5 post-IR relative to day 0. Full gene list and GO results in Supplementary Data 10–12. g Spatial CellChat analysis comparing day 0 (D0) and day 3 (D3). Spatial domains defined by unsupervised clustering. Changes in outgoing and incoming signaling strength per region. Full results in Supplementary Data 13. h–j CellChat analysis; h Differential signaling strength map showing enhanced stromal signaling at D3 post-IR (red) versus D0 (blue), measured by incoming and outgoing activity. i Differential signaling activity in the crypt stroma between day 0 and day 3 post-IR, assessed across the Secreted Signaling, Non-protein and ECM-Receptor interaction databases of CellChatDB. Pathways enriched at day 3 are in the upper right quadrant. j Total signaling strength (incoming + outgoing) across stromal regions for selected regeneration-associated pathways. k Dot plots of normalized log2 expression levels of key ligands and receptors across day 0 and day 3 post-IR. l Log2 expression of selected TGFβ, collagen, and retinoic acid signaling genes in day 0 and day 3 tissues, indicating shifts in pathway activation during regeneration. m Spatially restricted CellChat predictions recapitulate known regeneration-associated signaling pathways, supported by corresponding changes in ligand and receptor gene expression shown in dot plots. Created in BioRender. Ofer, R. (2026) https://BioRender.com/ivwn6ot. Scale bar: 100 µm. Source data are provided as a Source Data file.",
