      "figure": "Fig 2",
      "caption": "Fig 2\n\nEpistatic potentiators of antibiotic resistance evolution.\n\nA. High expression of efflux pumps accelerates the evolution of antibiotic resistance by increasing the phenotypic impact of mutations that alter antibiotic targets. This potentiator pathway can be blocked using efflux pump inhibitors. B. Mutations in metabolic genes potentiate the evolution of antibiotic resistance by establishing robust metabolic networks that minimize the fitness costs associated with antibiotic resistance mutations. This pathway of potentiation could conceivably be blocked by metabolic modulators. Figure created in BioRender. https://BioRender.com/jt7dem0.",
