      "caption": "FIGURE 1\n\nThe glioblastoma (GBM) microenvironment. The tumor microenvironment includes GBM tumor cells, tumor-associated microglia, M2 macrophages, and blood vessels. Microglia secrete growth factors and cytokines that drive tumor transition into the mesenchymal GBM phenotype. Anti-inflammatory M2 macrophages aid angiogenesis and tumor migration. The pro-tumor activity of the microglia is RAS-mediated. The tumor secretes cytokines and signaling molecules that cause macrophages to polarize into the pro-tumor M2 phenotype. Created in BioRender. Basole, U. (2026) https://BioRender.com/0xu9niy.",
