      "figure": "FIGURE 2",
      "caption": "FIGURE 2\n\nEffects of neurofibromin 1 (NF1) on RAS and ERK MAPK pathway. (A) The normal NF1 protein acts as a negative regulator of RAS and the ERK MAPK pathway, preventing overactivation and cell overproliferation. (B) In NF1-mutant glioblastoma, a loss-of-function mutation renders NF1 unable to regulate RAS, leading to RAS overactivation, cell overproliferation, and tumorigenesis. (C) Daraxonrasib, by forming a tricomplex with CypA and RAS-GTP (zoomed in), inhibits expression of genes further along the ERK MAPK pathway and reduces cell overproliferation. Created in BioRender. Basole, U. (2026) https://BioRender.com/xfmsr7y.",
