      "figure": "Fig. 3",
      "caption": "Fig. 3\n\nATP13A4 knockdown impairs astrocyte arborization.\n\na Schematic of the astrocyte-neuron co-culture assay used to assess astrocyte morphology. Created in BioRender. van Veen, S. (2026) https://BioRender.com/7x2wn63. b Representative astrocytes (green) transfected with shRNA targeting mouse/rat Atp13a4 (shAtp13a4) or scrambled control (shCtrl), co-cultured with WT neurons (invisible) for 48 hours. Scale bar, 50 μm. c Sholl quantification of astrocyte complexity for b. n = 72 (shCtrl), 71 (shAtp13a4) astrocytes from three independent experiments. d Representative GFP-labeled astrocytes (green) from WT and Atp13a4 KO mice following 48 hours of co-culture with WT neurons. Scale bar, 50 μm. e Sholl quantification for d. n = 102 (WT), 61 (KO) astrocytes from four (WT) or three (KO) independent experiments. f Representative shRNA-expressing astrocytes (green) with or without an shRNA-resistant mouse Atp13a4 (msAtp13a4) construct with N-terminal mCherry tag (red) after 48 hours co-culture with WT neurons. Scale bar, 50 μm. g Quantification for f. n = 60 astrocytes per condition from three independent experiments. h Representative shRNA-expressing astrocytes co-cultured with methanol-fixed WT neurons for 48 hours. Scale bar, 50 μm. i Quantification for h. n = 60 astrocytes per condition from three independent experiments. Mixed-effects ANOVA (c, e, i) with Tukey’s post-test (g). j Schematic of PALE (Postnatal Astrocyte Labeling by Electroporation). Plasmids were injected into the lateral ventricle of CD1 mice at late P0, followed by electroporation into radial glial stem cells, leading to sparse knockdown and labeling of cortical astrocytes. Created in BioRender. van Veen, S. (2026) https://BioRender.com/fhbbf7l. k Representative in vivo shRNA-transfected astrocytes (labeled with mCherry) at P21. Scale bar, 10 μm. l Quantification of in vivo astrocyte territory volumes by convex hull analysis in Imaris. Only astrocytes from V1 cortex were imaged and analyzed. n = 18 (shCtrl) or 22 (shAtp13a4) astrocytes from 3 (shCtrl) or 4 (shAtp13a4) mice, two-tailed nested t-test. Data shown as mean ± SEM, except in l, where individual territory volumes are shown as light grey data points, and the average territory volume per mouse is indicated in black (shCtrl) or red (shAtp13a4). Source data are provided as a Source Data file.",
