      "figure": "Fig. 2",
      "caption": "Fig. 2\n\nImbalance between protein production and lysosomal function in LBD. In a healthy brain, protein production and lysosomal degradation are in balance, as shown by an evenly weighted scale. In contrast, in an LBD brain, an increase in protein production overpowers/outweighs the degradation ability of a dysfunctioning lysosome, which could be what is leading to Lewy body pathology. It is thought that the dual impact of α-synuclein overproduction and reduced degradation is what leads to the accumulation of the protein (Created in BioRender. Watkins, M. (2026) https://BioRender.com/zr09emm)",
