      "authors": "Puja Banik; Addison C. Hill; Madison B. Schank; Yi Zhang; Juan Zhao; Jaeden S. Pyburn; Holly Orfield; Yuezu Wu; Mohammad J. Hajipour; Mohamed El Gazzar; Shunbin Ning; Jonathan P. Moorman; Zhi Q. Yao; Ling Wang",
      "figure": "FIGURE 6",
      "caption": "FIGURE 6\n\nConceptual model of CRISPR-Cas–mediated suppression of HBV replication in persistent HBV cell models based on experimental trends observed in this study. HBV life cycle (replication, transcription, translation, and viron production) in HepG2.2.15 and HepDE19 cells proceed as following: (1) viral RNAs (including pgRNA) are transcribed from cccDNA and HBV integrated DNA in the nucleus; (2) viral mRNAs are translated into viral proteins in the cytoplasm; (3) pgRNA is encapsidated into nucleocapsids, where reverse transcription generates rcDNA; (4) newly formed nucleocapsids acquire envelope proteins at the interface between the endoplasmic reticulum and the Golgi apparatus (5–6) mature virions bud into the secretory pathway and are subsequently released from the cell. CRISPR-based antiviral strategies target multiple stages of HBV replication and transcription: gRNA9/Cas9 and gRNA4/Cas12a mediate cleavage of HBV DNA in the nucleus, whereas gRNA7/Cas13 d degrades specific HBV RNA transcript in the cytoplasm. This schematic model is created in BioRender. Wang, L (2026) https://BioRender.com/8mcdj58.",
