      "authors": "Mahmoud Farahat; Ghazaleh DadashiZadeh; Zachary Ricciuti; Alexandra Pappas; Marc G. Jeschke",
      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3\n\nMechanisms of burn- and EV-mediated WAT browning\n\nSchematic representation juxtaposing burn-induced systemic responses with EV-mediated signaling in promoting white-to-beige adipocyte conversion. Burn injury stimulates catecholamine release, activating β-adrenergic signaling pathways that drive adipocyte reprogramming. Concurrently, burn-associated metabolic stress and inflammatory mediators, including interleukin-6 (IL-6) and lactate, contribute to browning processes. Exosomes derived from BAT and adipose stem cells carry regulatory miRNAs, including miR-193b, miR-328, miR-378a, miR-92a, and miR-191a-5p, which promote thermogenic programming in recipient white adipocytes. Cold exposure and exercise further influence EV cargo composition, enhancing pro-browning signaling. In addition, EV-mediated cross-talk contributes to immune modulation, including macrophage polarization, which may further support AT remodeling. Collectively, these pathways converge to induce WAT browning and metabolic reprogramming following burn injury. Created in BioRender. Jeschke, M. (2026)\nhttps://BioRender.com/w4i9xpr",
      "sourceUrl": "https://doi.org/10.1042/CS20260147",
      "license": "CC BY 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
      "condition": "Specific BioRender page explicitly licenses this Completed Graphic under CC BY 4.0; individual BioRender icons may not be extracted and redistributed separately. Article permissions cover the saved author text under CC BY 4.0. Selected excerpts and captions contain no identified credit requiring separate permission. Other article images are omitted. Image bytes unchanged; complete BioRender public PNG, no cropping or icon extraction. Original-language article paragraphs and linked captions converted from JATS XML to Markdown; styling removed, no OCR, translation or paraphrase. Graphic: Figure 3. Creator: Marc Jeschke. Provider: BioRender. Asset source: https://biorender.com/w4i9xpr. License evidence: https://app.biorender.com/citation/69c894c80959dfd42b8a430a. “Figure 3” created in BioRender. Jeschke, M. (https://BioRender.com/w4i9xpr) is licensed under CC BY 4.0. Article caption explicitly links to the complete BioRender asset; may correspond to a panel or construction sheet rather than the entire published figure.",
