      "id": "dec5a610",
      "diagram": "diagram/dec5a610.png",
      "class": "Conceptual Framework",
      "domain": "1",
      "title": "The cascade to pathogenicity in autoantibody-mediated CNS diseases",
      "authors": "Federico Montini; Elinor Wing; Max Herman; Sean J Pittock; Sebastian Lopez Chiriboga; Eoin P Flanagan; Sarosh R Irani",
      "figure": "Figure 4",
      "caption": "Figure 4\n\nTherapeutics with targeted mechanisms in autoantibody-driven disease. Schematic of choice, tailored mechanisms employed in autoantibody neurological disease. Many targeted therapeutics act chiefly in the periphery (left), downregulating the immune cells and pathways involved in autoantibody production and maintenance. Most of these (e.g. anti-CD19/20/38, CAR-T/CAAR-T) bind to membrane-bound proteins on pathogenic B-cell or ASC populations to decrease autoantibody production, while others like tocilizumab or FcRn inhibitors target soluble proteins or pathways of antibody recycling to decrease autoantibody production and maintenance, respectively. Natalizumab, acting at the blood–brain barrier (middle), is positioned between the peripheral and CNS compartments to prevent B- and T-cell ingress. Medications that act within the CNS at the target site (right) serve to prevent autoantibody–antigen interaction and the effector functions therein. Included on the bottom of the figure are emerging therapeutics, highlighting new uses of foundational therapies and emerging medications. *Limited effect on SLPCs, LLPCs. APC = antigen-presenting cell; CAR-T = chimeric antigen receptor T cell; CAAR-T = chimeric autoantibody receptor T cell; FcRn = neonatal fragment crystallizable receptor; HLA = human leucocyte antigen; IL- = interleukin; JAK = Janus kinase; LLPC = long-lived plasma cell; SLPC = short-lived plasma cell; VLA-4 = very late antigen-4. Created in BioRender. Montini, F. (2026) https://BioRender.com/4a73gbm.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://doi.org/10.1093/brain/awag158",
      "license": "CC BY 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
      "condition": "Specific BioRender page explicitly licenses this Completed Graphic under CC BY 4.0; individual BioRender icons may not be extracted and redistributed separately. Article permissions cover the saved author text under CC BY 4.0. Selected excerpts and captions contain no identified credit requiring separate permission. Other article images are omitted. Image bytes unchanged; complete BioRender public PNG, no cropping or icon extraction. Original-language article paragraphs and linked captions converted from JATS XML to Markdown; styling removed, no OCR, translation or paraphrase. Graphic: Figure 4. Creator: Fred Montini. Provider: BioRender. Asset source: https://biorender.com/4a73gbm. License evidence: https://app.biorender.com/citation/69ef5e162e6de252eaa342ae. “Figure 4” created in BioRender. Montini, F. (https://BioRender.com/4a73gbm) is licensed under CC BY 4.0. Article caption explicitly links to the complete BioRender asset; may correspond to a panel or construction sheet rather than the entire published figure.",
