      "figure": "Fig. 1",
      "caption": "Fig. 1\n\nGraphical and experimental timeline for maternal separation paradigm with preparation for immunohistochemical analysis. Pregnant dams arriving at embryonic day 14 (E14) were housed and fed ad libitum for their gestational period. Newborn pups in the experimental group were separated from their dams for 3 h daily from postnatal days (PND) 2 to 16, while the control group remained with their dams and were transported outside the vivarium. All animals were returned to the vivarium after separation events. Pups were weaned on PND 21 and subjected to the elevated plus-maze as a measure of anxiety on PND 39–40. Pups from the control and experimental groups were sacrificed on PND 42, and whole brains were harvested and prepared for downstream analyses. Figure created in BioRender.com; Betz A (2025a) https://BioRender.com/t19s794",
