      "caption": "Figure 4\n\nAtrioventricular canal (AVC) cardiomyocyte differentiation. Atrioventricular canal cardiomyocytes are generated though temporal exposure to both RA and a second stimulus of CHIR99021 to turn Wnt signaling back on. This specialized region, situated between the atria and ventricles, requires a mixture of signaling effectors to generate cells with transcriptomes comparable to those detected in vivo (e.g., BMP4 and Activin-A for ventricles, RA for atria). An organoid within a media well denotes a cardiac organoid. Created in BioRender. Argall, A. (2026) https://BioRender.com/r4zqkpi. Refs.: (A) [81]; (B) [82]; (C) [83]; (D) [71].",
