      "authors": "Xin Cheng; Yadong Zhang; Changli Qian; Erica Holdridge; Guruprasad Ananda; Tao Jiang; Jing Ni; Shaozhen Xie; Hao Gu; Renlei Ji; Elena V Ivanova; Marisa R Nucci; Zhe Wang; Kaifu Chen; Bose Kochupurakkal; Gordon J Freeman; Geoffrey I Shapiro; Joyce Liu; Panagiotis A Konstantinopoulos; Ursula Matulonis; Jean J Zhao",
      "figure": "Fig. 1",
      "caption": "Fig. 1\n\nCharacterization of the PIK3CAH1047R; Trp53−/−; Myc (APM) mouse model.\n\na Schematic illustrating the strategy used to generate the APM transgenic model. Created in BioRender. Gu, H. (2026) https://BioRender.com/1czjz4t. b Kaplan-Meier survival curves comparing APM mice with doxycycline-naïve transgenic controls (n = 6 mice per group). Survival differences were analyzed using the two-sided log-rank (Mantel-Cox) test. c RT-qPCR analysis of PIK3CAH1047R transgene, Trp53, and Myc expression in uterine epithelium (UE) and APM tumors. Data represent mean ± s.e.m.; n = 3 biologically independent tumors per group. Statistical significance was determined by two-tailed unpaired Student’s t-test. d Representative histology of primary APM tumors showing serous-like morphology (scale bar, 50 μm). Similar histological features were observed in n = 3 biologically independent tumors. e Representative longitudinal in vivo bioluminescence imaging of primary tumors during doxycycline treatment (Dox on) and following doxycycline withdrawal (Dox off) at the indicated time points after tumor cell injection (days 9, 12, 16, 19, and 26). Three representative mice (F301, F303, and F308) are shown. Luminescence is presented as photons per second per square centimeter (p/s/cm²). f Tumor volume changes in APM allografts treated with BYL719 (20 mg/kg) or vehicle. Data are presented as mean ± s.e.m.; n = 8 biologically independent tumors per group. Statistical significance between groups was determined by two-way ANOVA with multiple-comparison correction. g Immunoblot analysis of tumor lysates from mice treated with BYL719 or vehicle. Representative blots are shown; similar results were obtained in four biologically independent tumors per group. Source data are provided as a Source Data file.",
