      "figure": "Fig. 5",
      "caption": "Fig. 5\n\nFGFR inhibition enhances antigen presentation and reduces M2-like tumor-associated macrophages.\n\na TCGA analysis revealed an inverse relationship between FGFR expression and CD3D levels. RNA expression values (log2-transformed TPM) were obtained from the TCGA UCEC cohort (n = 527 tumors) and visualized using the R package pheatmap (https://www.cbioportal.org/study/summary?id=ucec_tcga_pan_can_atlas_2018). b Differential expression of HLA-A, HLA-B, and HLA-C in FGFR-amplified (n = 51) and non-amplified (n = 495) TCGA uterine endometrial carcinoma (UCEC) tumors. Each dot represents one independent tumor sample. RNA expression levels are shown as log₂-transformed TPM values. Horizontal lines indicate median values. Statistical significance was assessed using a two-sided Wilcoxon rank-sum (Mann-Whitney U) test. c Schematic of the in vivo experimental design. Created in BioRender. Gu, H. (2026) https://BioRender.com/956sotu. d–f Flow cytometry and RT-qPCR analyses of CD3+ and CD8+ T cells, M2-TAMs, and antigen-presentation gene expression in primary tumors, recurrent tumors, primary tumors overexpressing FGFR1/2/3, and recurrent tumors with FGFR knockdown. Each dot represents one biologically independent tumor. d Flow cytometric quantification of CD3⁺ cells, CD8⁺ cells, and M2-like TAMs in primary versus recurrent tumors; n = 8 biologically independent tumors for primary tumors and n = 10 for recurrent tumors. e Vector versus R1R2R3 tumors: flow cytometric analysis (left), n = 8 tumors for Vector and n = 10 tumors for R1R2R3; RT-qPCR analysis of antigen-presentation genes (right), n = 4 tumors per group. f Vector versus shR1R2R3 tumors: flow cytometric analysis (left), n = 8 tumors per group; RT-qPCR analysis of antigen-presentation genes (right), n = 4 tumors per group. Violin plots show the data distribution; the center line indicates the median. Data are presented as mean ± s.e.m. of biologically independent tumors. Statistical significance was determined by two-tailed unpaired Student’s t-test. g–i GSEA, RT-qPCR, and flow cytometry analyses demonstrating upregulation of antigen presentation-related genes and a reduction in M2-TAMs in FGFR-high recurrent Rec1 tumors following short-term lenvatinib treatment. g Schematic overview of experimental design. Created in BioRender. Gu, H. (2026) https://BioRender.com/ooq12da. h RT-qPCR analysis (left) of antigen-presentation genes in Rec1 tumors treated with vehicle control or lenvatinib; n = 6 tumors for the control group and n = 7 tumors for the lenvatinib treatment group. Data are presented as mean ± s.e.m. of biologically independent tumors. Statistical significance was determined by two-tailed unpaired Student’s t-test. Flow cytometric quantification of MHC I expression on CD45⁻ cells (middle) and M2-like TAMs (right); n = 6 tumors for the control group and n = 7 tumors for the lenvatinib treatment group. Each dot represents one independent tumor. Violin plots show the data distribution; the center line indicates the median. Statistical significance was determined by two-tailed unpaired Student’s t-test. i GSEA was performed using the GSEA software (v4.3.3, Broad Institute). Gene sets were evaluated using phenotype permutation testing. Normalized enrichment score (NES), nominal P values, and Benjamini-Hochberg FDR q values are shown. j, k Expression of antigen-presentation genes in EC cell lines and the DF4203 patient-derived organoid (PDO; FGFR1amp) following 7 days of FGFR inhibitor treatment. EN cells and DF4203 PDO were treated with lenvatinib (Len) or pemigatinib (Pem) as indicated. j RT-qPCR analysis of antigen-presentation genes in EN cells and DF4203 PDO. Experiments were independently repeated three times using the same cell line or PDO. For each independent experiment, RT-qPCR measurements were performed in technical triplicate. Data are presented as mean ± s.e.m. of n = 3 independent biological experiments. Statistical significance was determined by two-tailed unpaired Student’s t-test. k Flow cytometric analysis of surface B2M and HLA-A/B/C expression shown as fold change in mean fluorescence intensity (MFI). Experiments were independently repeated three times using the same cell line or PDO. Data represent mean ± s.e.m. from n = 3 independent experiments performed using the same cell line or PDO. Statistical significance was determined by two-tailed unpaired Student’s t-test. Illustration in j was created in BioRender. Gu, H. (2026) https://BioRender.com/uw4ak86. Source data are provided as a Source Data file.",
