      "caption": "Figure 2\n\nProposed effect of DiPT upon the firing rate of auditory nerve fibres (ANFs). The perception of low-frequency sounds relies on phase-locking mechanisms in which auditory nerve fibres synchronize their firing to the sound wave’s frequency (panel A). DiPT may modulate this phase-locking process, by delaying the firing of ANFs with respect to the incoming sound wave. Under the influence of DiPT, the same sound frequency will sound deeper (panel B). Created in BioRender. Hurst, A. (2026) https://BioRender.com/4m3f866.",
