      "figure": "Figure 4",
      "caption": "Figure 4\n\nOrganoid-derived stem cell platforms modeling tumor evolution and microenvironmental dynamics. Schematic diagram illustrating: (A) Sequential driver mutations (APC → KRAS → TP53 → SMAD4), introduced by CRISPR/Cas9, transform growth factor-dependent wild-type organoids into autonomous malignant organoids, recapitulating tumor initiation. (B) Tumor organoids exhibit a cancer stem cell (CSC) hierarchy, in which self-renewing CSCs generate progenitor and differentiated cells; persistence of CSCs under therapy drives relapse. (C) Co-culture with stromal and immune components models extracellular matrix (ECM) remodeling, cytokine signaling (TGF-β, IL-6), and PD-1/PD-L1/PD-L1-mediated immune modulation. (D) Oxygen and nutrient gradients establish hypoxic, metabolically reprogrammed niches, further enhanced by integration of perusable vasculature and organ-on-chip platforms. Created in BioRender.com (Version 2026); https://BioRender.com/2zpmx4f (accessed on 1 March 2026).",
