      "authors": "Ivonne Monter-Aldana; Adrian Pastor Lopez Monroy; Fernando Sanchez-Vega",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: CLS fusion model: The proposed model MMBV is a model of two streams, the ViT transformer (Dosovitskiy et al., 2021) for image, and the BERT transformer (Devlin et al., 2019) for text. The two transformers are connected by the CLS embedding in each block. The tokens of the text (Token_i) are the input for BERT, and the patches of the image (Patch_i) are the input for ViT. The h_CLS_{I−T} and h_CLS_{T−I} hidden states are not used for the input of the next self-attention block; instead, they are replaced by the h_CLS_img and h_CLS_txt versions from the transformer of the other modality.",
