      "caption": "Figure 1: Illustration of target-side data augmentation (DA) using a very simple example. A DA model is trained to estimate the distribution of possible translations y given a source ; and an observed target yi, and the MT model is trained on the sampled translations 9; from the DA model for each source i. Effectively training the DA model with the target yi, which is also a conditional input, can be challenging, but it is achievable after introducing an intermediate latent variable between the translation y and the condition yi.",
