      "title": "AMPERE: AMR-Aware Prefix for Generation-Based Event Argument Extraction Model",
      "authors": "I-Hung Hsu; Zhiyu Xie; Kuan-Hao Huang; Prem Natarajan; Nanyun Peng",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: An overview of AMPERE using an example from the ACE 2005 dataset. Given a passage and an event trigger, we first use an AMR parser to obtain the AMR graph of the input passage. The linearized AMR graph sequence will be encoded into a l-length prefix by an AMR encoder and an attention layer. Our generation-based EAE model equipped with the AMR-aware prefix then summarizes the event mentioned in the passage into a natural sentence that follows a pre-defined template in the prompt. The final arguments and the corresponding roles can be extracted from the generated sentence.",
