      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: An illustration of the training setup for the proposed method, HotelMatch-LLM. The top part encodes the query text using a small LM and aligns its embedding with the large LM, while the bottom part processes hotel images using a vision encoder (CLIP) to extract patch embeddings, averages them, aligns them with the large LM embedding size, and jointly passes them through the large LM to obtain the final hotel embeddings. Finally, a multi-task optimization is applied to train the HotelMatch-LLM retriever. dimcLIP, dimsLM, and dimLLM refer to the embedding dimensions of the CLIP, small LM, and large LM, respectively.",
