      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: Framework Overview of Our Evidence- and Graph-based RAG Distillation. Given a user query (top-left), the approach first retrieves and filters evidence by collecting relevant text snippets. Then, these references are fed into relationship filtering and ranking using an LLM and cosine similarity to yield high-quality ordered references. The resulting multigraph RAG structure is then converted into a simplified RAG graph (bottom-right), distilling crucial relationships and factual context, also extracts key entity pairs and links (e.g., “nymphs-→adults\"). Finally, SLMs leverage this distilled information, mitigating hallucination and transferring knowledge effectively.",
