      "authors": "Lirui Zhang; Huishuai Zhang",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: The DAS framework addresses the challenge of authorship attribution in large document corpora through a sequential progression strategy. The system operates in two core phases: (1) Coarse Filtering to narrow down candidate authors from thousands to a tractable subset, (2) Tournament-Style Attribution (TSA) that integrates LLMRank with dynamic weighting, multiple independent trials, and progressive elimination to iteratively reduce the candidate space and pinpoint the target author. This framework enables efficient analysis of long-form texts while maintaining computational feasibility at scale.",
