      "title": "Don't Trust: Verify -- Grounding LLM Quantitative Reasoning with Autoformalization",
      "authors": "Zhou, Jin Peng; Staats, Charles; Li, Wenda; Szegedy, Christian; Weinberger, Kilian Q.; Wu, Yuhuai",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: A pictorial illustration of Don't Trust: Verify. Left: starting from an informal statement, an informal solution is generated by a large language model. The informal statement and solution are then translated into their formal counterparts. Multiple informal solutions for each problem are generated with temperature sampling. Right: An automated theorem prover in the formal environment is used to verify formal solutions against formal statements step by step (indicated by [ATP]). The final answer is chosen using majority voting over only the verified solutions. In this example, Formal Solution #1 successfully proves Formal Statement #1. Formal Solution #2, however, fails to prove the \"only if' direction of Formal Statement #2.",
