      "title": "Discovering Object-Centric Generalized Value Functions From Pixels",
      "authors": "Somjit Nath; Gopeshh Subbaraj; Khimya Khetarpal; Samira Ebrahimi Kahou",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. The Object-Centric GVF Learning Framework: We have two parts a Question Network and a Main Network. The Question Network takes in a batch of inputs (st : : . St+d) and tries to predict GVF questions (cumulants) from each slot. Each of the cumulants corresponds to the slot outputs (c). The Main Network is an RL algorithm with GVF heads each of which is trained by the cumulants from the Question Network. For training GVFs, we use the Mean Squared TD Error (MSTDE) which depends on the cumulants discovered by the Question Network ( is the same as defined for the main task). The outputs of the GVFs are projected into the latent space where it is concatenated with the representation before normalization and action value prediction with respect to the main task.",
