      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. The framework of DMVG and data augmentation method. For data preprocessing, we initially select samples where the target view is not missing to serve as the training data. These training samples are then augmented as described in Section 3.4. During model training, a random noise is added to the target view, and the noisy target view along with all conditional views are fed into DMVG to fit this noise. In the model inference phase, the trained model is used to predict the missing samples of the target view. The detailed generation process is discussed in Section 3.3.",
