      "title": "Do Models Explain Themselves? Counterfactual Simulatability of Natural Language Explanations",
      "authors": "Yanda Chen; Ruiqi Zhong; Narutatsu Ri; Chen Zhao; He He; Jacob Steinhardt; Zhou Yu; Kathleen Mckeown",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. GPT-4 answers a human user's question and generates an explanation. In this example, what GPT-4 actually answers (right) is different from what the user would expect (left) based on the explanation. Therefore, the explanation misleads humans to form a wrong mental model of GPT-4 even though it is factually correct.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://proceedings.mlr.press/v235/chen24bl.html",
