      "domain": "0",
      "title": "Memoria: Resolving Fateful Forgetting Problem through Human-Inspired Memory Architecture",
      "authors": "Sangjun Park; Jinyeong Bak",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: Working memory retains the most recent information. Short-term memory also holds a fixed number of recent engrams. The number of engrams in long-term memory is not predetermined. The arrows in the diagram represent the connections between each engram. Each connection is directed and weighted. Those weighted edges are used for retrieval.",
