      "authors": "Yahong Zhang; Chenchen Fan; Donghui Chen; Congrui Li; Wenli Ouyang; Mingda Zhu; Junchi Yan",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. SPGM module overview: An LP/MILP instance is represented as a bipartite graph, where yellow and green nodes signify variables and constraints, respectively. A destroy and repair scheme is applied to a constraint vector Az. and the two rows of Xo indicate: i) its connections to variables; i) connection weights. These two rows undergo the forward noising and reverse denoising processes. The multiplication of these rows yields the new constraint Az.. The diffusion model is trained by reconstructing it back to the original one.",
