      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: Pipeline Comparison. Given a time series embedding/patch sequence a E RLxD, D > P where P is the patch size and forecasting horizon H: Non-Patch Based Models @ or Patch Based Models @ map it to the target sequence using a huge sequence-level linear layer Ws E R(L.D)× H; Our Patch-based Parallel Decoding aLLM4TS @ decodes each patch to the time domain using a small shared patch-level linear layer Wp E IRD× P without modeling temporal relationships among patches. Specifically, the parameters of our patch-based decoding layer are only LH (e.g., 0.34%, when P = 16, L = 64, H = 720), compared to the sequence-based decoding layer. Learning Paradigms. Instead of contrastive learning, masking reconstruction, and limited fine-tuning of the LLMs @, we adopt a forecasting-based two-stage pre-training task ② to better transfer the sequence modeling capabilities within LLMs to time series.",
