      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Overview of our proposed CM? framework. For a dataset with M modalities, we extract modality-specific embeddings zm via Encoderm and compute its Gaussian mixture model (GMM). We then model the marginal distributions and estimate the joint distribution using a copula family C. We sample 2m from its GMM if modality m is missing. The concatenated embedding z then passes through a 2-layer LSTM fusion module and MLP classifier to predict y. The ELBO for backpropagation can be obtained by aggregating the task-specific loss (e.g., cross-entropy loss) and the negative log-likelihood from the joint distribution.",
