      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1: (a) DeFoG enhances graph generation by introducing training-sampling decoupling, an orthogonal improvement within graph iterative refinement models, while preserving the sampling flexibility and inherent discreteness exploitation of prior SOTA models. (b) One node, x^(n), is selected to illustrate both noising and denoising processes. For noising, DeFoG follows a straight path from the one-hot encoding p₁ of the clean node to the initial distribution p₀. For denoising, a network parameterized by θ predicts the marginal distributions of the clean graph, there the node’s distribution p_{1|t}^{θ,(n)}(·|G_t) is used to compute its rate matrix R_t^{θ,(n)} and, subsequently, its probability at the next time point t + Δt.",
