      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. (a) Illustrating class geometry preservation in non-Euclidean hyperspherical spaces. The top row shows Gaussian diffusion, which fails to capture structural relations, whereas the bottom row demonstrates von Mises-Fisher (vMF)-based diffusion, effectively modeling directional uncertainty. Red and green arrows indicate forward and backward diffusion process, respectively. (b) Comparison of on the 3D sphere: Gaussian (top) vs. vMF (bottom). Gaussian distorts class boundaries, while vMF maintains the original geometry, preserving angularregions.",
