      "title": "On Understanding Attention-Based In-Context Learning for Categorical Data",
      "authors": "Aaron T Wang; William Convertino; Xiang Cheng; Ricardo Henao; Lawrence Carin",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. The left and middle figures depict the two self-attention heads, while the right-most figure reflects cross attention. A representative vector is shown at position i. The portion of the vector in blue remains the same at each layer k, and the portion in yellow is updated at each attention block. The sum of fi,k and △Ei,k at left and center is manifested via the skip connection. The form of the vector shown at right, for input to cross attention, depicts the updated fi,k+1, and the erased expectation, these the result of the preceding self attention. Cross attention (right) computes the expectation E(we)I fz, +1 and places it at its location within the vector (addition via skip connection). One complete attention block, with skip connections, is depicted in Figure 2.",
