      "id": "19370df9",
      "diagram": "diagram/19370df9.jpg",
      "class": "Algorithmic Framework",
      "domain": "0",
      "title": "Compositional Risk Minimization",
      "authors": "Divyat Mahajan; Mohammad Pezeshki; Charles Arnal; Ioannis Mitliagkas; Kartik Ahuja; Pascal Vincent",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. The additive energy classifier trained in CRM computes the logits for each group z = (y, a) by adding the energy components of each attribute via boradcasting. For the train logits, we add the log of the prior probabilities and a learned bias B(y, a) for the groups present in train data. At test time, the log prior term is replaced with the log of the test prior (if available, otherwise assumed to be uniform), and the biases for novel test groups, B* (y, a), are extrapolated using Eq.11. Finally, we obtain p(y, a|c) by applying softmax function on the adjusted logits. This adaptation from train to test is possible because of the additive energy distribution p(ly, a), which allows themodel to factorize the distribution into distinct components associated with each attribute.",
