      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. FairPFN Overview: FairPFN is a foundation model for causal fairness, pre-trained on synthetic datasets generated from sparse MLPs that represent SCMs with exogenous protected attributes (a). A biased dataset is created for each MLP/SCM and supplied as context to the transformer (b), with loss computed based on fair outcomes obtained by excluding the causal influence of the protected attribute (c). In practice, (d) FairPFN takes in only an observational dataset to predict fair targets by integrating over the simplest causal explanations forthebiased data.",
