      "title": "FLAM: Frame-Wise Language-Audio Modeling",
      "authors": "Yusong Wu; Christos Tsirigotis; Ke Chen; Cheng-Zhi Anna Huang; Aaron Courville; Oriol Nieto; Prem Seetharaman; Justin Salamon",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Comparison of traditional audio-language contrastive modeling (left) with the proposed Frame-wise Language-Audio Modeling (FLAM, right). Traditional models generate global embeddings for audio-text pairs and optimize an instance-wise contrastive objective. In contrast, FLAM integrates both instance-wise and fine-grained frame-wise contrastive objectives. Audio mixtures are synthesized from event instances, paired with text descriptions, and processed to produce frame-wise embeddings. Frame-wise contrastive learning explicitly aligns individual audio frames with textual event descriptions using event-specific scales and biases, enabling precise temporal localization of sound events.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/wu25ab.html",
