      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Illustration of TAR. Given graph go, we first conduct graph extrapolation to generate Gi. Next, we compute the classification loss, initially assigning equal sample weights to each node. Subsequently, we perform topology-aware reweighting. Specifically, nodes with higher loss values attract more sample weight through gradient flow from neighboring nodes. Finally, nodes with higher losses are assigned greater weights, while nodes with identical loss values exhibit different weights due to variations in their topological positions.",
