      "authors": "Samuele Marro; Jialin Yu; Emanuele La Malfa; Oishi Deb; Jiawei Li; Yibo Yang; Ebey Abraham; Sunando Sengupta; Eric Sommerlade; Michael J. Wooldridge; Philip Torr",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Overview of Critique-Resilient Benchmarking. Feasibility gating admits a question only if its self-answer a_A survives critique from all other models and no ill-posedness critique is upheld (Section 4). The claim type determines the outcome: an upheld incorrectness or obscurity critique is a benchmarker win, an upheld ill-posedness critique drops the question, and a rejected (or absent) critique is an answerer win. Only win/loss episodes enter the itemized bipartite Bradley-Terry fit, which yields answerer strength β and benchmarker strength α.",
