      "title": "Disentangling Latent Risk Pathways via Bayesian Hypergraph Inference",
      "authors": "Ding, Shengxian; Gao, Haonan; Liu, Pangpang; Tian, Xinyuan; Zhao, Yize",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Bayesian Hypergraph Pathway Inference Workflow. (a) Input data consist of patient covariates and multiple disease outcomes. (b) A latent disease hypergraph models higher-order structure via hyperedges, allowing diseases to participate in multiple pathways with uncertain existence and membership. (c) Risk factors act on hyperedges to induce structured effects across diseases, yielding disentangled attribution. Shaded regions denote posterior uncertainty. Bottom panels: Structured Variational Inference (left) preserves logical dependencies to learn the latent topology including hyperedge existence and membership (middle), while a repulsion prior (right) discourages redundant pathways to ensure a parsimonious and interpretable latent structure.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.07677",
