      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. FlashSinkhorn uses tiling to avoid materializing the n X m score matrix on slow HBM. Left: GPU memory hierarchy. SRAM (~20 MB, ~19 TB/s) is small but fast; HBM (～~80GB, ~1.5 TB/s) is large but slow. Middle: streaming f update (Algorithm 1). The outer loop (orange) stages a row block QI in SRAM with running LSE statistics; the inner loop (blue) streams K j tiles plus bias gj + j, forms the score tile on-chip, and writes fr to HBM after the inner loop completes. Right: streaming g update with Q, K swapped (bias fl + I). Hatched = SRAM tile, solid = HBM tensor; black arrows = HBM<>SRAM transfers, pink dashed = on-chip data flow.",
