      "class": "Algorithmic Framework",
      "domain": "0",
      "title": "Geometric Flow Grounding: A Unified Manifold Decoupling Framework for Dynamics Discovery and Verification",
      "authors": "Chang Yu; Yuxuan Luo; Yixuan Du; Yuqing Zhou; Siyuan Li; Jingbo Zhou; Jiawei Jiang; Zhen Lei; Stan Z. Li",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Geometric Flow Grounding: Intuition and Applications. (a) The Geometric Intuition. Standard dynamic models parameterize vector fields in the flat ambient space, leading to two critical failures: (1) Off-Manifold Rollout Drift, where discrete numerical steps (ct -→ t+1) can push the predicted trajectory (red dashed line) off the manifold; and (2) Smoothing Drift, where the model averages conflicting velocities in a neighborhood (Va , Ub) into an invalid vector c with a nonzero normal component. (b) Universal Applications. To resolve this, our framework employs a Neural Tangent Projection mechanism (center) that maps the latent velocity code Zu at latent state zs to the tangent velocity Utan. This geometric constraint serves as a unified foundation for three distinct tasks.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://proceedings.mlr.press/v306/yu26af.html",
      "license": "CC BY 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
