      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1 Overview of PAR. PAR comprises the autoregressive (AR) transformer T and the flow-based backbone decoder ve. During training, we downsample a backbone x E RLx3 into multi-scale representations {x', .. ., x}. AR transformer performs next-scale prediction, producing conditional embeddings (zl, . . , z\") from (bos, . . : , xn-1). The shared flow-based decoder learns to denoise backbones x' at each scale conditioned on z. At inference, PAR autoregressively generates x until the final structure x is constructed.",
