      "id": "2728b8be",
      "diagram": "diagram/2728b8be.jpg",
      "class": "Mechanism Diagram",
      "domain": "0",
      "title": "Skip a Layer or Loop It? Learning Program-of-Layers in LLMs",
      "authors": "Li, Ziyue; Li, Yang; Zhou, Tianyi",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Program-of-layers (PoLAR) for two different inputs. The D layers in a pretrained LLM define D functions fo, : . : , fD-1. Instead of calling them in a static fixed order from fo to fD-1, the dynamic inference of PoLAR executes an inputspecific program π = (ii, : . : , ik) that calls the functions with layer skipping and recurrence. PoLAR enables a training-free architecture of dynamic depth for different inputs, yielding diverse latent computations that cannot be fully covered by existing methods.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.06574",
