      "title": "Dissecting Multimodal In-Context Learning: Modality Asymmetries and Circuit Dynamics in modern Transformers",
      "authors": "Huang, Yiran; Roth, Karsten; Bouniot, Quentin; Xu, Wenjia; Akata, Zeynep",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Preliminaries in the multimodal setting. (a) The context consists of N triplets followed by the target query. The paired examples (ci, c2) from two modalities, with a shared label li, are generated from Gaussian Mixture Models (GMMs) by controlling within-class variation ei and ε2. (b) The distributional properties for the synthetic data. The burstiness B determines how often the class occurs in the context. Class frequencies follow a Zipfian distribution with exponents αi and aα2. (c) Evaluation distinguishes between IWL, where target queries belong to class seen during training while not in the context during evaluation, and ICL, where target queries are novel but in the context. A swapped-label condition further isolates ICL by permuting the labels.",
