      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Geometric interpretation of logical equivariance. (Left) A query q is associated with a score se (q) (e.g., log probability), and its gradient Φq = Vse(q) as a feature. Under the LPA, a local parameter update △ induces a score change approximated by the inner product: △s(q) = So+e(q) - Se(q) ～ <Φq, △). Logical consistency under direction-agnostic first-order propagation requires that any local parameter change enhancing q suppresses -q (i.e., △s(-q) = -△s(q)), which necessitates that the gradient vectors be anti-aligned (Φ-q ~ -q). (Right) This geometric requirement induces a commutative diagram where symbolic negation - in the query space corresponds to a linear inversion -I in the gradient feature space.",
