      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Overview. Top: We compare intrinsic dimensionality across reasoning strategies and evaluate how well it predicts generalization performance (c.f. Section 3). Middle (Green): To compute the intrinsic dimension of a reasoning strategy, we sweep varying LoRA parameter counts d and identify the minimum dint at which training accuracy crosses a common threshold T (described in Section 2.3). This Pareto frontier for a single strategy is shown across all strategies simultaneously in Figure 2. Right: We find a strong inverse correlation between intrinsic dimensionality and generalization performance (Section 4).",
