      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Estimating probabilities of rare harmful outputs. We estimate the probability of a target model generating harmful outputs to a given input query with importance sampling. Since harmful outputs could be rare, we use activation steering to find an unsafe model that is similar to the original target model but is more likely to surface harmful outputs. By sampling responses from the unsafe model and then reweighting them with respect to our target model, we can produce low-variance estimates of the probability of rare misaligned behaviors using fewer samples.",
