      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Overall framework of LSFLow. To enable expressive stochastic policies under hard combinatorial constraints, we shift policy learning to a continuous spherical cost-direction space and let a combinatorial optimization (CO) solver enforce feasibility (Section 3.1). Crucially, both policy and critic are learned directly in this latent cost space. We train the flow policy Te via weighted flow matching, using weights w α Q(s, c) predicted by a latent-space critic (Section 3.2). To stabilize cost-space critic learning under solver-induced discontinuities, we apply vMF smoothing by sampling ～ Kk(. I c) when constructing Bellman targets (Section 3.3).",
