      "title": "Learning Hamiltonian Flow Maps: Mean Flow Consistency for Large-Timestep Molecular Dynamics",
      "authors": "Winfried Ripken; Michael Plainer; Gregor Lied; Thorben Frank; Oliver T. Unke; Stefan Chmiela; Frank Noe; Klaus Robert Muller",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Hamiltonian Flow Maps (HFMs) for large timesteps in phase space. Top row: Existing approaches rely on trajectory data, typically generated using a teacher MLFF through sequential simulation with small timesteps. While this enables training large-timestep models via direct regression, the resulting models are limited to a fixed set of predefined timesteps that cannot be adjusted after training. Bottom row: Our approach learns continuous-time, large-timestep dynamics directly from decorrelated ab-initio samples, without requiring trajectories. The model supports arbitrary timesteps at inference. Our tailored loss combines force matching with a consistency constraint that enforces agreement of the predicted flow across different time horizons (see Section 4.2).",
