      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Overview of our approach for measuring language preference. We show both synthetic data generation and measurement method. Given an English query q and its K relevant evidence documents Den, we first translate the documents into multiple languages Dfr, Dar, Dko : : . (Step 1). We then generate a reference citation-supported report r for each query using q and Den (Step 2). The report r consists of sentence-level statements si, each paired with a single citation ID ci. For each r, we retain only statements that are verified (Step 3). Language preference is detected when the next token prediction accuracy for the correct citation ID decreases as the language of thecited documentis varied (Step 4).",
