      "caption": "Figure 1. Toy spiral manifold illustration of guidance geometry. Left: trajectories on a high-density spiral tube. Standard CFG (red) takes a Euclidean shortcut that leaves the manifold. A projected update (orange) stays closer to the manifold but progresses more slowly. MOG (blue) follows a geometry-aware direction that remains near the manifold while moving efficiently toward the condition. Top right: distance to the manifold over steps, highlighting off-manifold deviation under CFG. Bottom right: conditional energy over steps, showing that MOG reduces energy rapidly without leaving the high-density region.",
