      "id": "0d17ab38",
      "diagram": "diagram/0d17ab38.jpg",
      "class": "Algorithmic Framework",
      "domain": "0",
      "title": "Neuro-evolutionary Continual Reinforcement Learning",
      "authors": "Pengyi Li; Hongyao Tang; Yifu Yuan; Yan Zheng; Xin Xu; Jianye Hao",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. The overall framework of Nevo-CRL consists of five main steps: @ Reuse masks based on task semantic similarity and allocate additional parameters to construct a sparse mask population. @ Initialize the RL agent population based on the monolithic policy and apply the corresponding masks for subsequent learning. ③ The RL population interacts with the environment, and the collected experiences are stored in a shared replay buffer. @ Periodically select elite masks, perform importance-guided crossover, and prune unimportant elements in all masks to enhance sparsity. @ Update the generated masks to non-elite individuals and reuse parent parameters. Steps ③, @, and ? are iterated continuously. When a new task arrives, the process restarts from ①.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://proceedings.mlr.press/v306/li26gb.html",
