      "authors": "Matteo Tusoni; Giuseppe Masi; Andrea Coletta; Aldo Glielmo; Viviana Arrigoni; Novella Bartolini",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Schematic illustration of the proposed methodology. The original time series, here x₁ and x₂, are segmented into overlapping windows (step ❶). Then, for each window k, the amplitudes (a₁^k, a₂^k) and the exponents (λ₁^k, λ₂^k) of the power-law distributed spectra are computed (step ❷). These give rise to new, multi-dimensional, time series: (a₁, λ₁) for x₁ and (a₂, λ₂) for x₂ respectively (step ❸). Finally, multivariate Granger causality tests are performed on these new series, and the causal graph is constructed (step ❹).",
