      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Symmetry reveals coupled mean-shift inference in transformers. Left: Enforcing feature/label permutation symmetry layer by layer preserves the inference rule: we match predictions, response to query perturbations (local decision rule), and influential examples (context sensitivity). Middle: The symmetry constraint denoises weights into a canonical low-dimensional structure. Right: The resulting structure makes the forward pass readable as a closed-form iterative classifier (depth <> iterations), yielding a geometry-driven algorithmic motif inwhichfeaturesand labels co-evolve.",
